    model:"The pie chart illustrates what people in one city like most about living there, while the bar chart shows how satisfied residents are with four public services.\n\nOverall, friendly people are the most popular feature of the city, and healthcare is the service that residents are most satisfied with. In contrast, housing receives the lowest satisfaction rating.\n\nAccording to the pie chart, just over a third of residents (35%) say that the friendliness of local people is what they like best. Food is the second most popular answer, at 25 percent, followed by parks at 20 percent. Only 12 percent choose public transport, and the remaining 8 percent give other reasons.\n\nThe bar chart shows that 72 percent of people are satisfied with healthcare, and a slightly lower percentage (65%) are happy with schools. However, fewer than half of residents are satisfied with transport (48%), and only 30 percent are satisfied with housing."
