  writing:{
    type:"Task 2", min:250, time:"40 phút",
    prompt:"Nowadays, many young people take a year off between finishing school and starting university, in order to travel or work. What are the advantages and disadvantages of this?",
    plan:["Mở bài: paraphrase đề + nói bài sẽ bàn về ưu và nhược điểm","Thân 1: ưu điểm (trưởng thành hơn, kinh nghiệm làm việc, kiếm tiền) + ví dụ","Thân 2: nhược điểm (mất thói quen học, tốn tiền, chậm hơn bạn bè)","Kết bài: tóm tắt, có thể nêu ý kiến ngắn","Từ nối: Firstly, also, and, but, however, In conclusion"],
    model:"In many countries, it is becoming common for school leavers to take a gap year before they go to university. They often use this time to travel or to get a job. This essay will discuss the main advantages and disadvantages of this trend.\n\nThere are several advantages to taking a year off. Firstly, young people can become more independent and mature. When they travel alone or live away from home, they have to solve problems and manage their own money. Secondly, a gap year can give students useful work experience. For example, a student who works in a hotel for a year will improve their communication skills, and they can also save money for their studies.\n\nHowever, there are also some disadvantages. The biggest risk is that students may lose the habit of studying. After a year of working or travelling, it can be difficult to return to lectures and exams. In addition, travelling is expensive, so students from poorer families may not be able to afford it, and they might feel left behind. Finally, a gap year means that students will start their careers one year later than their friends.\n\nIn conclusion, a gap year can help young people to grow up and gain experience, but it can also make it harder to return to study and may be costly. I believe it is a good idea only if students have a clear plan for how they will use the time."
  },
  speaking:{
    tip:"Nếu nói sai, tự sửa ngay một cách tự nhiên: ‘I go… sorry, I went there last year.’ Dùng because để nêu lý do và so để nêu kết quả. Chú ý phát âm đuôi -ed.",
    p1:["Do you have a large family?","Who are you most similar to in your family?","What did you enjoy doing as a child?","Did you have a favourite teacher at school?"],
    p1sample:{q:"What did you enjoy doing as a child?",a:"When I was a child, I loved flying kites with my cousins, because our village had large open fields. We usually made the kites ourselves, so they often broke, but it was still great fun."},
    cue:{t:"Describe a person you admire.",pts:["who the person is","how you know him or her","what he or she has done"],end:"and explain why you admire this person."},
    p2sample:"I'd like to talk about my grandmother, who I admire more than anyone else. She was born in a small village in Nam Dinh and had a very hard childhood, because her family was poor and she had to stop school when she was twelve. Later, she moved to Hanoi and opened a small shop selling dried fruit. She worked from five in the morning until late at night, so she was able to send all four of her children to university. What I admire most is that she never complained. Even now, at eighty, she still gets up early, does exercise in the park and reads the newspaper every day. She taught me that hard work and a positive attitude are more important than luck.",
    p3:["Do people today have more interesting lives than people in the past?","What can young people learn from older generations?"],
    phrases:["…because…","…so…","Sorry, I mean…","When I was a child,…","I used to…","Later,…"]
  }
