    notes:"smartphone · present, 18th birthday\nevery day · maps, dictionary, video call parents\nwhy: learn English (apps, podcasts) · save time (bank, tickets) · stay in touch",
    p2sample:"The piece of technology I find most useful is my smartphone. My parents gave it to me as a present on my eighteenth birthday, so I've had it for about three years now. I use it every single day, probably for five or six hours. For example, I use the map app to find my way around the city, and I use a dictionary app whenever I see a new English word. It's useful for several reasons. Firstly, it helps me learn English, because I can listen to podcasts on the bus. Secondly, it saves me a lot of time. For instance, I can pay bills and buy train tickets without going anywhere, so I have more time to study. Finally, I live far from my parents, so I video call them every evening. Without my phone, I would feel much more lonely.",
